maria: can someone sanity-check the prose where I explain "when to fallback to a smaller model variant"? I recommended: 1) try trimming, 2) reduce temperature/length, 3) switch to a shorter variant (e.g., gpt-small) for >2s queuing.

sam: wording looks fine but call out quality regression risk and suggest a canary flag. Example sentence: "Prefer serving fallback only behind a canary or with explicit quality regression alerts enabled."

lee: also add the code path examples for Dedicated vs Hosted: Hosted get transparent 429s and we recommend client-side backoff; Dedicated may return graceful 503 for queued requests — include both in table.

